<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.3.4: Using Function Notation with a Real-World Example</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00888</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.3.4: Using Function Notation with a Real-World Example</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f6a358f4-ea3b-42ba-b602-8f0f01dda140</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Cool Down Activity</title>
      <para>An art museum opens at 9 a.m. and closes at 5 p.m. The function \(V\) gives the number of visitors in the museum \(h\) hours after it opens.</para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Explain what this statement tells us about the situation: \(V(1.25) = 28\).</para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>An hour and 15 minutes after the museum opened (at 10:15 a.m.), there were 28 visitors in the building.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Use function notation to represent each statement:
        <para>At 1 p.m., there were 257 visitors in the museum.</para>
        </para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(V(4)=257\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>At the time of closing, there were no visitors in the museum.</para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(V(8)=0\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
        <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
          <item>Use the previous statements about the visitors in the museum to sketch a graph that could represent the function.
    </item>
        </list>
      </list>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>When you have finished graphing, select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="Function. hours after opening time and number of visitors.">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_06_09_01.svg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
            </para>
            <para>Your graph should show points at \((1.25,28)\) and \((4,257)\), with or without lines connecting these points. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
